  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN277.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">talaimakaṉ piriviṉkaṭ talaimakaḷ paruvam kaṇṭu tōḻikkuc colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What SHE said to the confidante when seeing the season during the separation from HIM.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN277.1">
        <l><anchor n="1"/>taṇkatir maṇṭila maviraṟac cāayp</l>
        <l>pakalaḻi tōṟṟam pōlap pai<supplied>yeṉa</supplied></l>
        <l>nutaloḷi karappavu māḷviṉai tarumār</l>
        <l>tavali lu<supplied>ḷ</supplied>ḷamō ṭeḵ<supplied>ku</supplied>tuṇai yākak</l>
        <l>kaṭaiyalaṅ kurala vāḷvari yuḻuvai</l>
        <l>pēḻvāyp piṇaviṉ viḻuppaci nōṉā</l>
        <l>tirumpaṉañ ceṟumpi ṉaṉ<supplied>ṉa pa</supplied>rū<supplied>u</supplied>mayirc</l>
        <l>ciṟukaṭ paṉṟi varuti<supplied>ṟa</supplied>m pārkku</l>
        <l>mattamā raḻuvat tāṅka ṇalantalaip</l>
        <l>pottuṭai maratta pukarpaṭu nīḻa</l>
        <l>lāṟucel vampala racaiviṉa rirukku</l>
        <l>mīramil <supplied>ve</supplied>ñcura miṟantōr namvayiṉ</l>
        <l>vārā vaḷavai yāyiḻai kūrvā</l>
        <l>yaḻalakain taṉṉa kāmar tutaimayir</l>
        <l>maṉaiyuṟai kōḻi maṟaṉuṭaic cēvaṟ </l>
        <l>poripuri yeruttam pōlak kañaliya</l>
        <l>poṅkaḻaṉ muru<supplied>kki</supplied> ṉoṇkulai mānti</l>
        <l><supplied>citar</supplied>citarn tukutta cevvi vēṉil</l>
        <l>vantaṉ ṟamma tāṉē</l>
        <l>vārār tōḻinaṅ kāta lōrē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="2">Even though, gently, like the fading appearance by day</l>
        <l corresp="1">of the orb with cool rays, exhausted so that [its] shining ceases,</l>
        <l corresp="3">the light on [my] forehead vanishes, in order to give manly work </l>
        <l corresp="4">with an unperturbed heart, with [his] blade as a companion</l>
        <l corresp="12a-c">he traversed the hot desert without moisture/mercy,</l>
        <l corresp="11">where the travellers that go [that] way sit seeking rest</l>
        <l corresp="10">in the shade falling in patches from the trees that [still] possess [some] covering,</l>
        <l corresp="9">[their] crowns suffering, in that place of difficult thickets by the road,</l>
        <l corresp="5">where the sickle-striped tiger with a rumbling pretty voice</l>
        <l corresp="6">cannot endure the distressing hunger of [its] large-mouthed female</l>
        <l corresp="8">[and] looks out on the side where the small-eyed pig may come,</l>
        <l corresp="7">[its] fur thick like the fibres of a large palmyra frond;</l>
        <l corresp="12d-13c">before he  comes [back] to our side, you with choice jewels,</l>
        <l corresp="18d-19">summer itself has come, alas,</l>
        <l>the occasion when bees feed on, spread [and] scatter</l>
        <l corresp="17-18c">the bright bunches of the Palas tree, [its flowers] a flaring fire,</l>
        <l corresp="16">that flourished so as to resemble the sparkling neck</l>
        <l corresp="15">of the bold cock of the fowl staying by the house,</l>
        <l corresp="13d-14">with desirable dense plumage that sprouts like fire, [its] beak sharp.</l>
        <l corresp="20">He did not come, friend, our lover.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
